{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts@L111","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":111,"end":111}},"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":111,"end":111},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:3ccd20ba504c45d9af93b972af0e36d3d2c9e56db4d01423d2e2773bcee8f472","meta":{"text":"Inputs to {@link runMemoryCheck}. All git I/O is resolved by the CLI before calling."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts@L125","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":125,"end":141}},"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":125,"end":141},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a3fe6aa53fe1735cbee75b9ee057ed329855fe2e6a4170317548d37e19ff0569","meta":{"text":"Run the CI check gate over the PR's team proposals (PRD W4 exit gate, line 350). PURE — no git, no\nmodel. The caller (CLI) resolves the merge-base policy, the trusted-ref presence, and the receipts,\nthen this function decides:\n- **already-trusted**: the record's exact id (+ accept decision) is in the trusted ref → idempotent\nre-proposal, no further validation needed (PRD line 347 idempotence).\n- **newly-proposed**: the record is NOT in the trusted ref → pending until the PR merges; it MUST\ncarry admissible evidence (`verdicts.evidence !== 'invalid'`) + a gating receipt whose\n`policyHash` is the MERGE-BASE policy hash. A receipt pinning the PR's (changed) policy is a\nself-authoring violation (PRD line 276). A missing receipt is a hard violation (PRD line 346).\n- **refused**: the record's evidence is `invalid` → an agent cannot self-assert a pass (PRD 346).\nThe gate passes (`ok:true`) iff there are no self-authoring violations, no missing receipts, and no\nrefused records. `withoutTrustedRef` is reported but does NOT fail the gate (the repo simply has no\nteam-trusted memory yet — PRD line 279: memories \"remain pending rather than being trusted implicitly\")."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts@L26","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":26,"end":26}},"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":26,"end":26},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:54f5e0558e3e5bb8bb8327331041fb48ad24293c6f55a9cea78772cace9ed261","meta":{"text":"Why a team record is or is not trusted against the trusted ref."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts@L33","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":33,"end":33}},"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":33,"end":33},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:287843836e700ec7a562294ea8271d9980d9dfd1532e47817ca753f41bcc6ed3","meta":{"text":"A per-record trusted-ref verdict."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts@L40","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":40,"end":44}},"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":40,"end":44},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2cdf2e4fc7b57b66410ed4eb25a212eab69bb71f47271a53ad1bad77e297e59c","meta":{"text":"The subject-indexed form the CLI builds from the trusted ref: which record ids have an `accept`\ndecision whose `subject` is the record id. This is the unambiguous trusted-ref predicate (PRD line\n279: \"exact record AND decision blobs\")."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts@L52","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":52,"end":57}},"file":"packages/memory/src/trusted-ref.ts","span":{"start":52,"end":57},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:7a345573f06e7fa3450c8465d5c85e58c5ce128606608d4e2f3977edc6b51e2f","meta":{"text":"Derive team trust for a set of team records against the trusted ref (PRD line 279). A record is\n`trusted` iff (a) a trusted ref is configured AND (b) its exact `mem:` id is in the ref's record set\nAND (c) an `accept` decision for it is in the ref's decision set. Otherwise it is pending\n(`trusted:false`). `undefined` presence ⇒ no trusted ref ⇒ every record is `no-trusted-ref` pending."}}
